---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="AWS VPC Lab | Built By Raza"
  description="A production-style AWS VPC lab covering subnet design, routing, NAT, security and multi-AZ architecture."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">AWS LAB · 01</p>

      <h1>Production-Style AWS VPC</h1>

      <p class="intro">
        Designing a resilient AWS VPC with public and private subnets,
        controlled Internet access and a multi-AZ architecture.
      </p>

      <div class="meta">
        <span>Status: Planned</span>
        <span>Category: Cloud Networking</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">THE GOAL</p>
        <h2>Build the foundation correctly.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          The goal of this lab is to build a production-style AWS network
          rather than a single flat VPC.
        </p>

        <p>
          The design will use multiple Availability Zones, separate public
          and private subnets, controlled Internet access, routing and
          security policies.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">ARCHITECTURE</p>
      <h2>Target design.</h2>

      <div class="diagram-placeholder">
        Architecture diagram will go here
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section-label">DESIGN COMPONENTS</p>
      <h2>What this lab will include.</h2>

      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>VPC & IP Plan</h3>
          <p>Define CIDR space and subnet allocation for the environment.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Multi-AZ Subnets</h3>
          <p>Deploy public and private subnets across multiple Availability Zones.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Routing</h3>
          <p>Build route tables for public and private traffic flows.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Internet Access</h3>
          <p>Use an Internet Gateway and NAT architecture for controlled access.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span>05</span>
          <h3>Security</h3>
          <p>Compare Security Groups and Network ACL behavior.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span>06</span>
          <h3>Failure Testing</h3>
          <p>Test what happens when components or paths become unavailable.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">DESIGN DECISIONS</p>
        <h2>Why this architecture?</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          This section will document the reasoning behind subnet placement,
          routing, Internet access and high-availability decisions.
        </p>

        <p>
          The goal is not just to show what was configured, but why the
          architecture was built that way.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="section-label">LESSONS LEARNED</p>
        <h2>What changed after building it.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="copy">
        <p>
          This section will be updated after the lab is complete with
          troubleshooting notes, unexpected behavior and design improvements.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 120px 0 100px;
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: #6b7280;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 18px 0 24px;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5.5rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 8px 0 20px;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 14px 0 8px;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #4b5563;
  }

  .meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 28px;
    color: #6b7280;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .section {
    padding: 95px 0;
  }

  .alt {
    background: #f7f7f8;
  }

  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 80px;
  }

  .copy p {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: #4b5563;
  }

  .diagram-placeholder {
    min-height: 360px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    margin-top: 35px;
    border: 2px dashed #d1d5db;
    border-radius: 16px;
    color: #9ca3af;
    background: #fafafa;
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 22px;
    margin-top: 45px;
  }

  .card {
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: white;
  }

  .card span {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #9ca3af;
  }

  .card p {
    color: #6b7280;
  }

  @media (max-width: 850px) {
    .split,
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .split {
      gap: 24px;
    }
  }
</style>